WEBVTT

00:01.590 --> 00:04.560
♪ It seems today that all you see ♪

00:04.590 --> 00:08.200
♪ Is violence in movies and sex on TV ♪

00:08.220 --> 00:11.430
♪ But where are those good
old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.460 --> 00:14.430
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.460 --> 00:17.930
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.970 --> 00:21.540
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.620 --> 00:23.160
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:23.180 --> 00:24.860
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.980 --> 00:30.220
♪ He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:34.820 --> 00:36.850
Is it me, or does David Ortiz

00:36.890 --> 00:39.050
look just like the mom on Good Times?

00:39.090 --> 00:41.500
- Oh, Peter, that's racist.
- Well, no. Look.

00:44.060 --> 00:45.330
I take it back.

00:45.360 --> 00:47.600
That's not racist. That's just accurate.

00:47.630 --> 00:49.760
Hey, guys, guess who's got the keys

00:49.820 --> 00:52.030
to a speedboat just sitting
down at the station?

00:52.070 --> 00:53.670
How'd you get a speedboat?

00:53.700 --> 00:55.940
Well, it's a funny story.

00:58.480 --> 01:00.460
That was a funny story.

01:00.580 --> 01:01.940
Especially the funny part.

01:01.980 --> 01:03.880
You really delivered on your promise.

01:03.910 --> 01:06.320
All right, who's up for waterskiing?!

01:06.340 --> 01:08.100
- Hell yeah!
- All right!

01:08.160 --> 01:09.280
Yeah, let's do it!

01:09.320 --> 01:12.090
Oh, that sounds amazing! I love boats.

01:12.120 --> 01:13.450
Boats are my thing.

01:13.490 --> 01:16.900
Anything to get out on the open
water, enjoy the salt air.

01:16.980 --> 01:18.020
Oh, they're already gone.

01:18.140 --> 01:19.536
No, you didn't widen enough.

01:19.560 --> 01:21.700
But you still can't come.

01:25.970 --> 01:28.770
Good evening, Quahog. Just
parking. Be there in a sec.

01:30.840 --> 01:32.240
Our top story:

01:32.280 --> 01:35.660
authorities have uncovered a
mob-run prescription drug ring

01:35.680 --> 01:37.210
targeting Goldman's Pharmacy.

01:37.250 --> 01:39.850
The scam involved
fraudulent prescriptions

01:39.860 --> 01:41.180
submitted for dead people.

01:41.220 --> 01:43.540
Pharmacist Mort Goldman failed to report

01:43.600 --> 01:44.890
to authorities for questioning.

01:44.920 --> 01:48.220
A $10,000 bounty has been
offered for his return.

01:48.260 --> 01:50.840
$10,000? That's a lot of money.

01:50.880 --> 01:52.600
Could be our money, Brian.

01:52.720 --> 01:54.600
We could find Mort. Easily.

01:54.630 --> 01:56.700
Besides, we haven't
done anything together

01:56.740 --> 01:59.430
since our confusing two-host talk show.

01:59.470 --> 02:02.040
So, Chris Pratt, I hear
you have a new movie out.

02:02.110 --> 02:03.470
So, Chris, you're from Seattle?

02:03.510 --> 02:05.440
Chris, what was it like
working with Amy Poehler?

02:05.500 --> 02:07.860
Hey, Chris, anything you can
tell us about Guardians 3?

02:07.920 --> 02:09.060
- Chris! Chris!
- Chris! Chris!

02:09.080 --> 02:10.440
- Chris Pratt, always a pleasure.
- Well, that's all the time

02:10.460 --> 02:12.096
- we have with Chris Pratt.
- Take it away,

02:12.120 --> 02:13.920
- multiracial modern band!
- retro swing guys!

02:13.960 --> 02:17.280
Guests of

02:17.320 --> 02:18.559
- The Stewie Griffin Show stay
- The Brian Griffin Show stay

02:18.560 --> 02:20.360
- at the Essex House.
- at the W Times Square.

02:25.800 --> 02:27.760
Waterskiing!

02:27.800 --> 02:29.800
- All right!
- Water-sitting!

02:37.470 --> 02:39.000
You got to cut to the right.

02:39.060 --> 02:42.010
No, no, it's counterintuitive.
You got to cut left.

02:42.040 --> 02:43.480
I know how to drive.

02:49.550 --> 02:51.680
Stop looking at us!

02:59.060 --> 03:02.100
Ugh! Maybe we won't be
going waterskiing today.

03:02.130 --> 03:03.180
Shut up, Joe.

03:03.220 --> 03:05.830
Hey, you want some help?
I do this all the time.

03:05.870 --> 03:08.200
[BLEEP] Get back in your
car with your wife!

03:10.860 --> 03:14.660
When you're going backwards,
everything's the opposite.

03:14.760 --> 03:17.080
Oh, really? Thanks, driving instructor.

03:36.000 --> 03:37.970
I feel like everyone watching knows

03:38.000 --> 03:41.000
I'm incapable of pleasing
my wife sexually.

03:42.440 --> 03:44.740
Now cut the wheel. Cut the wheel!

03:44.770 --> 03:46.820
No, the other way!

04:02.560 --> 04:04.890
Ah, hell, we're gonna
be on the Internet.

04:13.140 --> 04:14.900
You know what? Screw it.

04:20.780 --> 04:22.580
Let's boat!

04:27.620 --> 04:29.280
Cleveland, aren't you waterskiing?

04:29.320 --> 04:31.900
- I don't like getting wet.
- Oh, come on.

04:31.980 --> 04:34.260
What's the worst that could happen?

04:59.220 --> 05:02.550
Mort must have panicked after the
pharmacy bust and fled town.

05:02.590 --> 05:04.190
If we're gonna collect our ten grand,

05:04.220 --> 05:06.250
we need to figure out where he went.

05:08.490 --> 05:10.960
Crap. His computer is
password-protected.

05:10.990 --> 05:14.060
Um, try "Such heat this day."

05:14.100 --> 05:15.460
Nope.

05:15.500 --> 05:18.380
How about "This fish is
cold, I want a refund"?

05:19.140 --> 05:20.670
No.

05:20.700 --> 05:23.270
