you start thinking straight.

14:41.230 --> 14:43.230
Use it on yourself, Joe.

14:43.270 --> 14:45.420
There's more than one
bullet in here, Joe.

14:45.740 --> 14:48.220
Yeah, on second thought, maybe
you should hold this, Cleveland.

14:49.110 --> 14:50.910
Are you really gonna just sit there

14:50.940 --> 14:55.010
after all the crap white people
have given you your whole life?

14:55.050 --> 14:58.410
You know, maybe you
should hold this, Peter.

14:58.450 --> 15:01.820
Peter, you could get free tacos with me.

15:02.950 --> 15:04.020
It worked!

15:06.960 --> 15:09.440
_

15:11.960 --> 15:14.870
Quagmire, why the hell would
you want to kill yourself?

15:14.910 --> 15:17.260
Yeah, who ever heard of a
depressed ventriloquist?

15:17.340 --> 15:20.500
You want to know why? Because
I can't do this anymore.

15:20.680 --> 15:22.140
My life is over.

15:22.180 --> 15:25.610
I tried to adjust, but it's impossible.

15:25.650 --> 15:28.150
Come on, Quagmire, it's not impossible.

15:28.190 --> 15:30.590
You want impossible,
try eating local pizza

15:30.620 --> 15:32.250
with a guy from New York.

15:33.280 --> 15:34.700
You call this pizza?

15:34.740 --> 15:36.320
We do here, yes.

15:39.960 --> 15:42.300
All right, Brian, I
negotiated to get Mort

15:42.380 --> 15:43.930
- back from the mob.
- How?

15:43.970 --> 15:46.160
I told them Mort gave us his flash drive

15:46.260 --> 15:48.170
with enough evidence to
put them all in jail.

15:48.210 --> 15:51.110
We're going to trade it for
Mort and collect our money.

15:51.140 --> 15:54.310
And I also ordered an
extra slice of pie.

15:54.440 --> 15:56.680
Because you know how many
times we live, Brian?

15:56.710 --> 15:58.180
Once.

15:58.220 --> 16:00.250
Once.

16:11.030 --> 16:13.660
- Hey, Dad.
- I'm so sorry, Glenn.

16:13.700 --> 16:15.060
Stop staring, Cleveland!

16:15.100 --> 16:16.900
I can support his lifestyle

16:16.930 --> 16:18.830
and still think it's weird!

16:18.870 --> 16:21.700
- Thank you, Cleveland.
- Have a blessed day!

16:23.140 --> 16:26.020
Believe me, Glenn, I know
what you're going through.

16:26.080 --> 16:27.260
No, you don't.

16:27.320 --> 16:29.680
You had yours surgically
removed in a hospital.

16:29.710 --> 16:31.510
I had mine bitten off by a shark!

16:31.550 --> 16:33.780
I'm not allowed to go
into the ocean anymore.

16:33.820 --> 16:36.400
The doctor says I can't
get seawater in it.

16:36.990 --> 16:38.760
I also have Crohn's disease.

16:39.080 --> 16:40.180
They're unrelated.

16:40.200 --> 16:41.260
Why are you here, Dad?

16:41.290 --> 16:42.920
I knew you were down in the dumps,

16:42.960 --> 16:44.930
so I brought you something
to cheer you up.

16:44.960 --> 16:46.930
A Yeti cooler?

16:46.960 --> 16:49.200
- That is kind of rad.
- No, that's mine.

16:49.230 --> 16:50.480
Your gift is inside.

16:54.140 --> 16:55.420
Is that your...?

16:55.610 --> 16:58.170
Yes, Glenn. It's my penis.

16:58.210 --> 17:00.610
After my surgery, I
kept it in my freezer.

17:00.640 --> 17:03.750
Next to a snowball from the
winter, if you can believe that.

17:03.780 --> 17:05.560
I want you to have it.

17:05.780 --> 17:08.840
I... I can't take your penis, Dad.

17:09.020 --> 17:10.280
Please, take it.

17:10.340 --> 17:12.520
If you don't, I'm just gonna
give it to Paul Ryan.

17:12.560 --> 17:14.360
I don't know what to say.

17:14.390 --> 17:15.940
Thank you.

17:16.490 --> 17:17.790
Weird.

17:17.830 --> 17:20.620
Proud of you guys, but weird.

17:26.740 --> 17:29.170
Okay, has everyone washed their hands?

17:29.210 --> 17:31.580
Me neither, but going
forward, let's try.

17:31.840 --> 17:33.640
I'm so nervous for Quagmire.

17:33.680 --> 17:36.710
I know, but it's nice that they
served hot dogs for the surgery.

17:36.750 --> 17:38.340
There it is! Give me that!

17:45.060 --> 17:48.020
Nurse, you put it on there. I'm not gay.

17:52.930 --> 17:54.960
The operation was a success.

17:55.000 --> 17:57.760
- Congratulations, Quagmire!
- Thanks, guys.

17:58.030 --> 18:00.940
And, Dad, I don't know how to thank you.

18:00.970 --> 18:03.980
You've given me the greatest
gift I could ever ask for.

18:04.210 --> 18:07.140
- I love you, son.
- I love you, too.

18:12.620 --> 18:15.050
- So, will it work, Dr. Hartman?
- Oh, yes.

18:15.090 --> 18:17.920
I'm not sure about urination
or sex, but otherwise, yes.

18:17.950 --> 18:19.350
So, how you feeling?

18:19.390 --> 18:21.420
I'm actually in extreme pain, Doc.

18:21.460 --> 18:23.620
It's like knives are
stabbing into my crotch.

18:23.660 --> 18:25.060
Don't worry, that'll go away

18:25.100 --> 18:27.240
once you fill your prescription
at Goldman's Pharmacy.

18:27.260 --> 18:29.560
- Mort's is closed.
- Oh. Oh, yeah.

18:29.600 --> 18:31.930
Cool tie-in with the
other story, though.

18:31.970 --> 18:34.740
I'm trying to get more involved
in the writing this season.

18:34.770 --> 18:37.380
In fact, I think Family Guy
should be more of a dramedy.

18:37.610 --> 18:39.270
- What's a dramedy?
- Well, for one thing,

18:39.310 --> 18:41.910
the scenes don't have to end with jokes.

18:48.780 --> 18:51.020
- You got the flash drive?
- Yep.

18:51.220 --> 18:53.590
All the information that
could put you away forever.

18:53.620 --> 18:55.420
Now, again, I don't know why we couldn't

18:55.460 --> 18:56.790
have done this by Dropbox.

18:56.830 --> 18:59.130
I mean, I don't mind coming
here to a parking lot...

18:59.160 --> 19:00.559
I had to get Mort anyway... but

19:00.560 --> 19:02.399
Dropbox would've saved you time.

19:02.400 --> 19:04.730
And you wouldn't have to
mail me back my flash drive.

19:04.770 --> 19:06.470
What do you mean, mail it back?

19:06.500 --> 19:09.480
You were planning to
keep it? It's 64 gigs!

19:09.600 --> 19:11.910
I bought the coverage. You're
not getting the coverage.

19:11.940 --> 19:14.660
Hi, guys. I'm a pharmacist.

19:14.840 --> 19:18.400
Ugh, Mort is so hard to write for.

19:18.650 --> 19:19.750
Okay, give us Mort.

19:19.780 --> 19:21.760
My mailing address is
in the flash drive.

19:21.990 --> 19:24.460
FBI! Freeze!

19:28.440 --> 19:29.720
What the hell is this?

19:33.260 --> 19:35.330
Thanks for your cooperation, Mr.
Goldman.

19:35.370 --> 19:37.900
Wait a minute. You were
working with the Feds?

19:37.930 --> 19:39.330
Absolutely.

19:39.370 --> 19:41.099
When I heard there was a reward,

19:41.100 --> 19:43.480
I immediately turned myself in.

19:43.510 --> 19:45.740
So you guys get bupkis.

19:45.780 --> 19:47.400
I'm a pharmacist.

19:49.280 --> 19:52.220
Well, Brian, we may not
have gotten the $10,000,

19:52.240 --> 19:53.360
but it'll be a joy

19:53.440 --> 19:55.096
to hear no more Jewish talk

19:55.120 --> 19:56.120
for a long while.

19:56.290 --> 19:58.950
"Brian and Stewie laugh.
The image freezes.

19:58.990 --> 20:00.390
The end."

20:00.420 --> 20:02.560
Ah, that was a good day's work.

20:02.590 --> 20:04.160
I've earned this.

20:06.430 --> 20:09.230
Little shot of the ol'
Sorkin genius juice.

20:16.490 --> 20:18.830
So, Quagmire, how's the
new rod holding up?

20:18.860 --> 20:21.430
Yeah, you know. Good, pretty good.

20:21.470 --> 20:24.300
I've been having a lot of sex. Um...

20:24.340 --> 20:26.900
My dad didn't mention there's a
four-inch mole on the left side.

20:26.940 --> 20:28.240
- What?
- Uh-huh.

20:28.270 --> 20:30.340
It's, like, the size of a 50-cent piece

20:30.370 --> 20:33.380
- and a dime kissing each other.
- Yikes. Frightening.

20:33.440 --> 20:35.210
Yeah, some gals find it off-putting.

20:35.250 --> 20:38.410
I try to tell them it's my dad's
old penis, but that, um...

20:38.450 --> 20:40.580
that just tends to make it worse.

20:40.620 --> 20:42.580
But the girls that stay are just great.

20:42.620 --> 20:44.420
Well, I'm happy for you, Quagmire.

20:44.460 --> 20:47.190
Don't be. Anyway, I got to take a leak.

20:47.220 --> 20:48.980
Well, I'm just glad our friend's

20:49.040 --> 20:50.440
back to his old self.

20:50.460 --> 20:52.340
Yeah, seems he hasn't missed a beat.

20:52.460 --> 20:55.560
It's great that we can be there
for each other in trying times.

20:55.600 --> 20:58.040
What's that noise?

20:58.600 --> 21:01.450
That's the sound of peeing
out your daddy's wiener.

21:01.460 --> 21:06.460
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru